"'''Bad Guy'''" (stylized in [[all lowercase]]) is a song by American singer-songwriter [[Billie Eilish]] and the fifth single from her debut studio album, ''[[When We All Fall Asleep, Where Do We Go?]]'' (2019). It was released on March 29, 2019, by Darkroom and [[Interscope Records]]. The song was described by media as [[dance-pop]], [[electropop]], and [[pop-trap]], with minimalist instrumentation. In the lyrics, Eilish taunts someone for being tough while suggesting that she is a more resilient [[wiktionary:bad guy|bad guy]] than he is. Eilish wrote "Bad Guy" with its producer and her brother [[Finneas O'Connell]]. Different versions of the song include a collaboration with the Canadian singer [[Justin Bieber]] and a cover by [[Dove Cameron]]. 

Upon release, "Bad Guy" received positive reviews and topped the US ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Billboard Hot 100|Hot 100]] and 16 other international charts including Australia, Canada and New Zealand, while peaking at number two on the [[UK Singles Chart]]. In the US, it ended the record-breaking 19-week run of "[[Old Town Road]]" by [[Lil Nas X]] featuring [[Billy Ray Cyrus]]. "Bad Guy" has received several [[Music recording certification|certification]]s, including a tenfold platinum award from the [[Australian Recording Industry Association]] (ARIA) and a Diamond certification from the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA). "Bad Guy" is the tenth most streamed song in Apple Music history. The song received several awards, including [[Grammy Award for Record of the Year|Record]] and [[Grammy Award for Song of the Year|Song of the Year]] at the [[62nd Annual Grammy Awards]].

[[Dave Meyers (director)|Dave Meyers]] directed the music video, which depicts Eilish involved in several activities such as wild dancing, suffering a nosebleed and sitting on the back of a man doing push-ups. Reviewers noted the video for its [[camp (style)|camp]] elements and eccentric imagery.

